// LEVEL: 1
// DEPENDENCE: ./src
// Regression: -e claims "Regular expressions are supported" (manual and -h).
// Glob-compatible patterns work (c.cj, test*.cj, sub/), but regex-only
// syntax silently fails: c\.cj (escaped dot) and [s]ub/c\.cj (char class)
// do NOT exclude src/sub/c.cj. This case pins the regex promise with the
// regex-only discriminator 'c\.cj'. NOTE: if the fix direction is to change
// the docs to wildcard-only semantics instead of implementing regex, update
// this case to assert the documented wildcard behavior.
// EXEC-PIPE: %lint -f ./src -e "c\.cj" -c %cangjieDir/tools -m %cangjieDir 2>&1 | compare %f
// ASSERT: regex .*a\.cj:10:5:.*warning.*G\.VAR\.01: Prefer immutable variables when the value of the variable 'count' does not change\.
// ASSERT: regex .*test_x\.cj:10:5:.*warning.*G\.VAR\.01: Prefer immutable variables when the value of the variable 'count' does not change\.
// ASSERT: regex-not .*sub[/\\]c\.cj:10:5.*
